.TH CCACHE_CAPACITY 3 "2026-10-31" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
ccache_capacity \- get the capacity of an LRU cache (type-inferred wrapper)
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/clrucache.h>

ccache_capacity(cache);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Type-inferred wrapper for clrucache_capacity(). It takes the same arguments
and gives the same result; clrucache_capacity(3) has the full contract.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
cache  Cache handle to query
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
The capacity, which is always >= 1 for a valid handle. It is 0 when
cache is CCACHE_NULL, and 0 when cache is a stale handle that a
call already destroyed.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR clrucache_capacity (3)
